@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName DejaVu Sans
skinparam defaultFontSize 16
skinparam ArrowColor #087C61
skinparam ClassBorderColor #087C61
skinparam ClassBackgroundColor #EAF7ED
skinparam ActorBorderColor #192D3D
skinparam UsecaseBackgroundColor #EAF7ED
skinparam UsecaseBorderColor #087C61
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #EAF7ED
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #087C61
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF7ED
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #087C61
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF6DF
skinparam NoteBorderColor #C5AB62
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam dpi 160
actor "Any user" as User
actor "Administrator" as Admin
participant "Django auth" as Auth
participant "accounts.signals" as Sig
participant "Users page:\nUserRoleView /\nUserStatusView" as View
participant "events.record_event" as Rec
database "AccountEvent" as DB
== Sign-in ==
User -> Auth : POST /accounts/login/
alt Valid and active account
 Auth -> Sig : user_logged_in
 Sig -> Rec : login (account, address)
else Wrong password, unknown name or deactivated
 Auth -> Sig : user_login_failed
 alt Typed name matches an account
  Sig -> Rec : failed login (account name, address)
 else No matching account
  Sig -> Rec : failed login (blank name, "Unknown username")
 end
end
Rec -> DB : Insert event (password never stored)
== Account change on the Users page ==
Admin -> View : POST role or active, plus next
View -> View : Admin check, not own account,\nonly a superuser edits a superuser,\nrole must be a valid choice
alt Rejected
 View --> Admin : Error message, no change
else Accepted
 View -> DB : Save role or is_active
 View -> Rec : role changed / activated / deactivated
 Rec -> DB : Insert event (actor, account, detail)
 View --> Admin : Back to the Users page (same-site next only)
end
note over Sig, DB
Five or more failed logins for one account in 24 hours raise a warning
on the system report. It is a prompt to review, not proof of an attack.
There is no automatic lockout.
end note
@enduml
